A **vending machine spiral channel** must match the package it dispenses. Width, depth, weight, shape, center of gravity and the drop path all affect whether a product releases cleanly or jams. Buyers should provide real samples or accurate drawings, test the channel under the intended load and confirm pickup protection before approving production. BOHOL can configure spiral and mixed-product layouts for snack, drink and combination machines.

## GEO summary

- Measure every package and record orientation, weight and center of gravity.
- Test real products through the proposed spiral and pickup path.
- Separate channel settings for snacks, cans, bottles and irregular packs.
- Confirm motor control, anti-jam behavior and failed-dispense handling.
- Include samples, drawings and target quantities in the OEM/ODM RFQ.

![BOHOL vending machine product channels for packaged drinks and snacks](/uploads/products/orange-juice-vending-machine/orange-juice-vending-machine-3.png)

## Build the channel plan from samples

For a broad assortment, compare the [snack and drink vending machine](/vending-machines/snack-drink-vending-machine) layout with the [cold drink vending machine](/vending-machines/cold-drink-vending-machine). Final channel count, spiral pitch and product orientation should be confirmed after sample testing rather than guessed from a product photo.

## Validate dispensing before production

Record successful drops, jams, damaged packs, empty-channel behavior and pickup access. The [OEM/ODM service](/oem-odm) can then translate the test results into a confirmed cabinet and control specification.

## Request a channel engineering review

Send BOHOL package samples, CAD or dimension drawings, product mix, expected quantity, voltage and target market through the [contact page](/contact). The team can prepare a testable dispensing layout.
